### Network generation


2G 3G, 4G, 5G.

You've heard these terms used, you know that your smartphone is 5G, and that's probably about it.

What is it, and how does affect dumbphones?

As cellphones, and then later on smartphones, gained adoption, and entirely new types of online platforms appearred and took off, the load on wireless networks got heavier, and they therefore had to evolve to keep up.

Millions were invested in improving the underlying technologies powering the cellphone towers, giving us newer generations of cellular tech powering our phones.

The second generation brought text messaging, cellular data, and encrypted calls.

Third gen cellular brought significantly faster data speeds, simultaneous voice calls and data on some networks, and video calls.

Gen four gave us even faster speeds, higher quality voice calls, and more reliable simultaneous voice and data.

The next round upped the data speeds again and lowered the latency.

For short we just called these 2G, 3G, 4G, and 5G.




